      <data key="e_quote">Spanish    Academic qualifications ➢ 1996 Master of Laws (LL.M), Harvard Law School – United States  ➢ 1993 License spéciale en droit européen, Institut d’études européennes,  Université Libre de Bruxelles – Brussels, Belgium  ➢ 1992 Licenciatura en Derecho, Facultad de Derecho, University of Valencia –  Valencia, Spain  Professional experience  in the European  Commission  ➢ Since 1 January 2026: Deputy Director-General in the Directorate-General for  Defence Industry and Space (DEFIS) – Brussels, Belgium  ➢ 07/2024 – 12/2025: Deputy Director General for Health responsible for  Directorates B, C and D, DG Health and Food Safety (SANTE) – Brussels, Belgium  ➢ 12/2020 – 06/2024: Director for Digital Society, Trust and Cybersecurity, DG  Communications Networks, Content and Technology (CNECT) – Responsible for e- Health policies, e-privacy, e- identity and cybersecurity.</data>
