      <data key="e_source_url">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephane_Sejourne</data>
      <data key="e_quote">It was in Argentina, in 2001, while the country was sinking into an economic crisis, that he decided to engage in politics within the Socialist Party, “because it was the only organization that had an international structure.” After obtaining his baccalaureate in 2005, he returned to France, entered the University of Poitiers and obtained a bachelor’s degree in economic and social administration (AES), then a master’s degree in public law and a master’s degree in European law in 2011.</data>
    </edge>
